{"name":"Awning Red","hex":"#90413e","fetched":"2026-10-11","looked":{"definitions":[{"term":"awning","whole":false,"parts":[{"part":"Noun","definitions":["A rooflike cover, usually of canvas, extended over or before any place as a shelter from the sun, rain, or wind.","That part of the poop deck which is continued forward beyond the bulkhead of the cabin."]}],"link":"https://en.wiktionary.org/wiki/awning"},{"term":"red","whole":false,"parts":[{"part":"Noun","definitions":["The color of the setting sun, blood, and strawberries; the color which is evoked by the longest visible wavelengths (between about 625–740 nm), and a primary additive color.","A revolutionary socialist or (most commonly) a Communist;  a Bolshevik, a supporter of the Bolsheviks in the Russian Civil War."]},{"part":"Adjective","definitions":["Of a red hue.","Having an orange-brown or orange-blond colour; ginger."]}],"link":"https://en.wiktionary.org/wiki/red"}],"entries":[{"title":"Awning","blocks":[{"text":"An awning or overhang is an architectural projection attached to and supported by a building, consisting of a lightweight frame with a covering. It is used to provide shade and protection from the weather, and may also serve decorative or signage functions. It is typically composed of canvas woven of acrylic, cotton or polyester yarn, or vinyl laminated to polyester fabric that is stretched tightly over a light structure of aluminium, iron or steel, possibly wood or transparent material. The configuration of this structure is something of a truss, space frame or planar frame. Awnings are also often constructed of aluminium understructure with aluminium sheeting. These aluminium awnings are often used when a fabric awning is not a practical application where snow load as well as wind loads may be a factor."}],"image":"https://thumb.wikimedia.org/wikipedia/commons/thumb/8/8d/Baden-Baden_Kurmuschel.jpg/330px-Baden-Baden_Kurmuschel.jpg?utm_source=en.wikipedia.org&utm_campaign=api&utm_content=thumbnail","link":"https://en.wikipedia.org/wiki/Awning","wikidata":"Q29053350"},{"title":"Red","blocks":[{"text":"Red is the color at the long wavelength end of the visible spectrum of light, next to orange and opposite violet. It has a dominant wavelength of approximately 625–750 nanometers. It is a primary color in the RGB color model and a secondary color in the CMYK color model, and is the complementary color of cyan. Reds range from the brilliant yellow-tinged scarlet and vermillion to bluish-red crimson, and vary in shade from the pale red pink to the dark red burgundy."}],"image":"https://thumb.wikimedia.org/wikipedia/commons/thumb/c/cf/Delicious_fresh_strawberries_%284735910403%29.jpg/330px-Delicious_fresh_strawberries_%284735910403%29.jpg?utm_source=en.wikipedia.org&utm_campaign=api&utm_content=thumbnail","link":"https://en.wikipedia.org/wiki/Red","wikidata":"Q3142"}],"images":[{"srcset":"https://thumb.wikimedia.org/wikipedia/commons/thumb/7/72/Diwan-i-Khas%2C_Red_Fort%2C_Delhi_with_red_awnings_or_shamianas%2C_in_1817.jpg/500px-Diwan-i-Khas%2C_Red_Fort%2C_Delhi_with_red_awnings_or_shamianas%2C_in_1817.jpg?utm_source=en.wikipedia.org&utm_campaign=parser&utm_content=thumbnail 1x, https://thumb.wikimedia.org/wikipedia/commons/thumb/7/72/Diwan-i-Khas%2C_Red_Fort%2C_Delhi_with_red_awnings_or_shamianas%2C_in_1817.jpg/1280px-Diwan-i-Khas%2C_Red_Fort%2C_Delhi_with_red_awnings_or_shamianas%2C_in_1817.jpg?utm_source=en.wikipedia.org&utm_campaign=parser&utm_content=thumbnail 2x","src":"https://thumb.wikimedia.org/wikipedia/commons/thumb/7/72/Diwan-i-Khas%2C_Red_Fort%2C_Delhi_with_red_awnings_or_shamianas%2C_in_1817.jpg/500px-Diwan-i-Khas%2C_Red_Fort%2C_Delhi_with_red_awnings_or_shamianas%2C_in_1817.jpg?utm_source=en.wikipedia.org&utm_campaign=parser&utm_content=thumbnail","alt":"Diwan-i-Khas, Red Fort, Delhi with red awnings or shamianas, in 1817","link":"https://en.wikipedia.org/wiki/File%3ADiwan-i-Khas%2C_Red_Fort%2C_Delhi_with_red_awnings_or_shamianas%2C_in_1817.jpg"},{